{"id": "EUVD-2026-108721", "enisaUuid": "b5a68ea2-8d5b-3982-8e5c-9b1f55dd2193", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndrm/nouveau/gsp: add SEC2 to GA100 chip table\n\nThe booter-load and booter-unload firmware run on the SEC2 falcon.\nDuring tu102_gsp_oneinit(), the booter constructor needs device->sec2\nto access the SEC2 falcon.\n\nWithout the .sec2 entry, device->sec2 is NULL and this dereference\ncrashes during GSP-RM boot.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:31:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:31:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/feb1ad41281aed00e8a741942e56a1cd774e8342", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f29267ace04283e76f92a74d9a7f4fcfcb32f484", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/604d0efb17cc0dd197e089134736ac2698d5fca7", "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-98875"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98875", "GHSA-4mjf-hj34-55hg"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "070205eb-2b57-3272-b5a1-e9becc0892be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.6.158"}, {"id": "3105af08-1c1c-3fde-a8a9-25355124854e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "6702c972-6ff0-3038-acfc-956bd194272c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <604d0efb17cc0dd197e089134736ac2698d5fca7"}, {"id": "83a6b1ef-a960-3175-9915-ea7821af6087", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <6.18.53"}, {"id": "88651148-422f-3c1a-a508-f058962b36ac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <f29267ace04283e76f92a74d9a7f4fcfcb32f484"}, {"id": "9f876cf8-28d3-3a02-8708-1fbefe7a3664", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "b0f0130f-0ea9-33a5-b2d6